From: Pingouin
Subject: [PATCH] ui/cocoa: the user picks the displays the VM uses (⌃⌥D), remembered

What: in full screen, upstream gave every other Mac display a window of its
own (pingouin-cocoa-displays.patch). Now only displays chosen for the VM do.
The choice is remembered per display (its UUID) in a JSON file the app edits
too (PINGOUIN_DISPLAYS_CHOICES: {"<UUID>": true|false}; changes are picked up
live). A display with no choice yet gets a notice once a run ("X connected.
Press ⌃ + ⌥ + D to use it for <vm>."); one chosen yes is used at once, with a
notice. ⌃⌥D on a display in use stops using it (remembered no); anywhere else
it uses the next display not in use (the one under the pointer first).
The notices take no click and no focus: the pointer goes through to the VM.
Why: the user decides when the VM takes a second screen; a choice made once
holds, whether the display is plugged in before or after the VM starts.
Upstream: Pingouin only.
